# Base system
base
linux
# The linux-firmware metapackage pulls ~773 MB of blobs, and firmware is already
# compressed, so squashfs cannot claw any of it back - it lands on the ISO
# roughly 1:1. Only the subpackages an x86 machine can actually use are listed,
# and the list is also what keeps the ISO under GitHub's 2 GiB per-file
# release-asset limit: the baked model eats about a gigabyte of that budget.
# Dropped: qcom (Snapdragon SoC - phones/ARM laptops), mellanox, qlogic, nfp and
# liquidio (datacenter NICs and Fibre Channel HBAs), other (the long tail of
# obscure devices; the common Wi-Fi families below are kept), marvell (legacy
# laptop Wi-Fi) and cirrus (laptop smart-amp DSP - a headless box has no speakers).
linux-firmware-intel
linux-firmware-atheros
linux-firmware-realtek
linux-firmware-mediatek
linux-firmware-broadcom
linux-firmware-amdgpu
linux-firmware-radeon
linux-firmware-nvidia
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
mkinitcpio-nfs-utils
sudo
polkit
dbus
# checkupdates, for the LiteAI tools: package_query lists pending updates
# against a copy of the sync database, so the AI never has to run `pacman -Sy`
# - which would leave the real database half-synced and the machine one command
# away from a partial upgrade.
pacman-contrib

# Live medium / installer tooling
arch-install-scripts
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
gptfdisk
parted
rsync
efibootmgr
grub
syslinux
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
util-linux

# Networking
networkmanager
wpa_supplicant
wireless-regdb
openssh
wget
curl
ca-certificates

# The local AI stack.
#
# nodejs and npm run pi (the coding agent the machine boots into) and the
# LiteAI MCP server. llama.cpp itself is NOT a package: scripts/fetch-llamacpp.sh
# stages a prebuilt upstream binary into /opt/llama.cpp, which keeps builds
# reproducible and free of AUR dependencies. base-devel, cmake and python exist
# so the machine can rebuild llama.cpp with GPU support later - the documented
# upgrade path for anyone whose hardware deserves better than the CPU build.
nodejs
npm
cmake
base-devel

# Tools the AI (and the human) work with
git
python
python-pip
man-db
man-pages
less
nano
vim
zip
unzip
tree
htop
fastfetch
ripgrep
fd
bash-completion
openssl
gnupg
